# A private message opens a query; our own echoed message opens the
# target's. A user's notice goes to its query if there is one, else to the
# console. Queries stay below channels in the sidebar.
! welcome echo-message
< :irc.test 005 textual CHANTYPES=# :are supported by this server
< :dave!d@h PRIVMSG textual :pm one
? buffers = console dave
? line dave <dave> pm one
< :textual!u@h PRIVMSG carol :hi carol
? buffers = console dave carol
? line carol <textual> hi carol
< :erin!e@h NOTICE textual :psst
? buffers = console dave carol
? line console -erin- psst
< :dave!d@h NOTICE textual :notice dave
? line dave -dave- notice dave
< :textual!u@h JOIN #x
> MODE #x
? buffers = console #x dave carol
< :irc.test NOTICE textual :server says
? line console -irc.test- server says
# A NICK renames the query, unless one with the new nick is open.
< :dave!d@h NICK carol
? buffers = console #x dave carol
< :dave!d@h NICK david
? buffers = console #x david carol
? line david dave is now known as david
? registered textual
